    "content": "The Risk-Based Testing plan for **Kitchen-me** is saved at [`docs/RISK-BASED-TESTING-PLAN.md`](docs/RISK-BASED-TESTING-PLAN.md). Summary below; the file is the canonical deliverable for downstream agents.\n\n---\n\n## Plan at a glance\n\n**Risk posture:** Elevated-but-manageable — revenue-critical checkout/inventory flows, GDPR (EU/UK), complex thin/full account merge, and MOCK payment logic dominate exposure.\n\n| Level | Count | Risk IDs |\n|-------|------:|----------|\n| **Critical** | 4 | R-01 Stock overselling, R-02 Payment/orphan orders, R-03 Incorrect totals, R-04 Account merge data loss |\n| **High** | 12 | R-05 through R-16 (PCI, auth abuse, RBAC, GDPR, XSS, coupons, refunds, cancel/restock, OAuth/phone, email, tracking) |\n| **Medium** | 8 | R-17 through R-24 |\n| **Low** | 3 | R-25 through R-27 |\n\n**Test execution order:** R-01 → R-02 → R-03 → R-04 → R-05–R-08 (blockers) → R-09–R-16 → Medium/Low.\n\n**Coverage floors (Critical modules):** Unit ≥90% line; Integration ≥85% of acceptance criteria; E2E 100% of Critical journeys (min 5).\n\n**Critical/High scenarios:** 80 Given/When/Then scenarios across R-01–R-16 (5 each).\n\n**Runtime Validation Map:** 43 alert rows mapping Critical/High risks to Sentry, PostHog, Mixpanel, Datadog, and Vercel Analytics with explicit breach thresholds.\n\n**Deferred this cycle:** Real Stripe, subscriptions, multi-address book, written reviews, abandoned-cart emails, gift cards, live chat, SMS transactional, full self-service returns, per-country EU shipping, advanced coupons, Hebrew email parity, third-party pen test.\n\n---\n\nThe full document includes all seven required sections with complete tables, scenarios, coverage targets, deferred risks, and the mandatory **Runtime Validation Map** as the final section. No `risk_categories` block was found in the workspace domain pack; risks were derived from the Discovery Brief, 69 user stories, and OWASP / ISO 25010 e-commerce heuristics."
